From 2bb9c1d9d5950578eccaf738a68f8441f0df2bd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:55:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LibrariesManager: libraries opened with RTLD_NODELETE

The destructor of the manager, called at the exit of the program, closed
the libraries of behaviours. A library of the openmp backend of the
generic-parallel interface then unloaded libgomp, when no other library of
the program used it, while the threads of its pool were still waiting
actively on its barrier: they executed code which was no longer mapped,
and the program crashed at its exit (segmentation fault in
gomp_barrier_wait_end, called by gomp_thread_start; with a program whose
output is redirected to a file, the last lines written are also lost).
Seen on Adastra (MI300A partition) with BatchIntegrationTest,
HeatTransferKernelsTest and MicromorphicKernelsTest of mfem-mgis, where no
other library loads libgomp at the start of the program; LD_DEBUG=files
shows libgomp unloaded by the destructor. The libraries are opened with
RTLD_NODELETE, which keeps them and their dependencies loaded.
---
 src/LibrariesManager.cxx | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/LibrariesManager.cxx b/src/LibrariesManager.cxx
index 64656c5..2de462a 100644
--- a/src/LibrariesManager.cxx
+++ b/src/LibrariesManager.cxx
@@ -110,7 +110,19 @@ namespace mgis {
 #if (defined _WIN32 || defined _WIN64) && (!defined __CYGWIN__)
     return ::LoadLibrary(TEXT(l.c_str()));
 #else
+    // The libraries are never unloaded (RTLD_NODELETE), nor their
+    // dependencies: the destructor of the manager, called at the exit of the
+    // program, would otherwise unload a library of behaviours whose runtime
+    // still has threads, such as the pool of threads of libgomp started by
+    // a library of the openmp backend of the generic-parallel interface,
+    // when no other library of the program uses this runtime. Its threads,
+    // waiting actively on the barrier of the pool, then execute code which
+    // is no longer mapped (segmentation fault at the exit of the program).
+#ifdef RTLD_NODELETE
+    return ::dlopen(l.c_str(), RTLD_NOW | RTLD_NODELETE);
+#else  /* RTLD_NODELETE */
     return ::dlopen(l.c_str(), RTLD_NOW);
+#endif /* RTLD_NODELETE */
 #endif /* (defined _WIN32 || defined _WIN64) && (!defined __CYGWIN__) */
   }    // end of load_library
 
-- 
